<Project>

  <!--
    Standalone Broiler.HTML builds use the Graphics checkout nested inside that submodule.
    Root builds instead use the canonical top-level Graphics checkout, which for the Win32
    demo means the src/ layout Broiler.Graphics publishes today.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)' == '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.HTML\Source\Broiler.HTML.Graphics.Win32.Demo\Broiler.HTML.Graphics.Win32.Demo.csproj'">
    <ProjectReference Remove="..\..\Broiler.Graphics\Broiler.Graphics.Windows\Broiler.Graphics.Direct2D.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Graphics\src\Broiler.Graphics.Windows\Broiler.Graphics.Direct2D.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Broiler.HTML reaches the top-level Broiler.Media checkout through the pre-src/ layout
    ("Broiler.Media\Broiler.Media.Image.Managed\"). That layout only ever existed inside the
    Broiler monorepo, which vendored Broiler.Media as a plain directory; the standalone
    Broiler-Platform/Broiler.Media repository has published its projects under src/ since its
    first commit, so the reference as written cannot resolve against the submodule.

    Delete this block once Broiler.HTML follows Broiler.Media into src/ and the gitlink here
    is bumped past that commit.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)' == '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.HTML\Source\Broiler.HTML.Image\Broiler.HTML.Image.csproj'">
    <ProjectReference Remove="..\..\..\Broiler.Media\Broiler.Media.Image.Managed\Broiler.Media.Image.Managed.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Image.Managed\Broiler.Media.Image.Managed.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Broiler.Graphics carries its own Broiler.Media gitlink, and that gitlink trails the
    top-level one. Left alone, a root build compiles Broiler.Graphics against the nested
    checkout while Broiler.Media.Image.Managed compiles against the top-level one, and both
    emit an assembly called Broiler.Media.Image into the same output directory. Whichever
    copy wins the copy decides whether ImageCodec.DecodeAsync is abstract, so the loser's
    codecs fail to load: "Method 'DecodeAsync' in type 'PngImageCodec' ... does not have an
    implementation."

    Point Broiler.Graphics at the canonical top-level checkout so a root build produces one
    Broiler.Media.Image, one Broiler.Media.Video, one Broiler.Media.Video.Windows and one
    Broiler.Media. Standalone Broiler.Graphics builds keep using its nested checkout.

    Delete this block once the Broiler.Graphics gitlink for Broiler.Media is bumped to the
    commit this repository pins and the two cannot drift apart again.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)' == '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Graphics\src\Broiler.Graphics\Broiler.Graphics.csproj'">
    <ProjectReference Remove="..\..\Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Image\Broiler.Media.Image.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Image\Broiler.Media.Image.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)' == '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Graphics\src\Broiler.Graphics.Windows\Broiler.Graphics.Direct2D.csproj'">
    <ProjectReference Remove="..\..\Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Video\Broiler.Media.Video.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Remove="..\..\Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Video.Windows\Broiler.Media.Video.Windows.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Video\Broiler.Media.Video.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Broiler.Media\src\Broiler.Media.Video.Windows\Broiler.Media.Video.Windows.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
